# Core

Core types and algebraic structures for LOGOS programs.

## Definition

## Note
The success-or-failure type: an `Ok` carries the value, an `Err` carries the error. Construct with `a new Ok with value x`, match with `When Ok (v):`.

A Result of [T] and [E] is either:
    An Ok (value: T).
    An Err (error: E).

## Note
A maybe-value: `some x` when present, `none` when absent. Inspect with `When Some (v):` and `When None:`.

An Option of [T] is either:
    A Some (value: T).
    A None.

## Note
The generic growable sequence behind `Seq of T` — built in; this line only names it.

A List of [T] is a generic collection.

## Note
The generic key-value table behind `Map of K to V` — built in; this line only names it.

A Map of [K] and [V] is a generic collection.
